User space                  Kernel driver                  Hardware
-----------                ----------------                ----------
mmap()        ───────────►  DMA buffer allocated
ioctl(START) ───────────►  Program DMA registers  ──────► DMA engine
                                │
                                │ interrupt
                                ▼
                         ISR marks frame ready
read frame directly from mmap buffer (NO COPY)




/*--------------------------------------------------------------------*/

main.c

Open device

/dev/mydma created by the driver.

mmap()

Maps the DMA buffer into user space (zero-copy)

ioctl(IOCTL_START_STREAM)

Starts DMA transfer in the driver

read()

Blocks until the driver signals frame-ready via IRQ

process_frame()

Example of accessing the DMA buffer directly

Cleanup

munmap() and close()

gcc -o main main.c
/*--------------------------------------------------------------------*/

For dma_ioctl:

Device Tree node (REQUIRED)

Your driver assumes this DTS node exists:

mydma@40000000 {
    compatible = "vendor,mydma";
    reg = <0x40000000 0x1000>;
    interrupts = <GIC_SPI 42 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
    dma-coherent;
    status = "okay";
};